.\" distributing a binary linked against libx264.
.TH CASTMIRROR-GUI 1 "2026-11-18" "CastMirror 1.0.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
castmirror-gui \- GTK 4 desktop front end for CastMirror
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B castmirror-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B castmirror-gui
is the GTK 4 + libadwaita desktop application for CastMirror. It has no custom
command line options; all state is persisted in
.I ~/.config/castmirror/config.json
and shared with
.BR castmirror (1).
.PP
The window is organised into four views:
.TP
.B Cast
LAN receiver list with model glyphs, rescan, Add by IP, and remove-saved-device
actions, a Screen or Window selector, the six quality preset cards (Auto, High,
Balanced, Smooth, Game, Cinema), an inline target bitrate cap slider (1\-25 Mbps),
and the primary Cast action in the bottom bar.
.TP
.B Live session
Real-time status hero banner with Freeze, Mute TV, Game Mode, and Cinema Mode
quick controls; 5-stage session pipeline diagram; health banner; 9 live
telemetry cards with FPS, video bitrate, RTT, and packet-loss sparklines; the
8-rung adaptive quality ladder; and the session activity timeline.
.TP
.B Settings
Video bitrate cap, capture frame rate, computer sound toggle, host speaker
mute, Opus audio quality (64\-256 kbps), target playout delay (100\-400 ms),
camera latency HUD overlay toggle, LAN subnet scan, Force X11 capture, Force
software encode, system tray icon and close-to-tray toggles, desktop
notifications, color scheme (System default, Light, Dark), and the hardware and
network self-test wizard.
.TP
.B Logs
Minimum log-level selector (Debug, Info, Warn, Error), text filter, copy last
100 lines (JSON sidecar when present, or current view), copy all, open log
folder, and clear view.
.SH SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Return
Start or stop casting.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Rescan LAN for Cast devices.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+1 ", " Ctrl+2 ", " Ctrl+3 ", " Ctrl+4
Switch between Cast, Live session, Settings, and Logs views.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.TP
.B F1
Show the About dialog.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_FORCE_SOFTWARE_ENCODE=1
Force FFmpeg libx264 software encoding even where VAAPI hardware encoding is
available.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_VAAPI_DEVICE=/dev/dri/renderD129
Use a specific VAAPI render node instead of probing
.IR /dev/dri/renderD* .
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_FORCE_X11=1
Force X11 capture instead of the Wayland xdg-desktop-portal ScreenCast path.
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_CONFIG_DIR=/path/to/dir
Redirect the configuration and log directory, as for
.BR castmirror (1).
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_VERBOSE_JSON=1
Enable structured NDJSON diagnostic breadcrumbs in
.IR castmirror.ndjson .
.TP
.B CASTMIRROR_CSS=/path/to/style.css
Load a custom GTK CSS stylesheet instead of the bundled theme CSS.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/config.json
Persisted settings, shared with the CLI.
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/castmirror.log
Rotating engine debug log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/castmirror-session.log
Per-session debug log overwritten on each cast.
.TP
.I ~/.config/castmirror/castmirror.ndjson
Structured NDJSON diagnostics when
.B CASTMIRROR_VERBOSE_JSON=1
or
.B verbose_json_logging
is enabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR castmirror (1),
.BR xdg-desktop-portal (1),
.BR pipewire (1)
.SH NOTES
On Wayland the desktop portal asks which screen or window to share when a
session starts. System tray integration requires the Ayatana AppIndicator
library at build time; without it the application still runs and simply has no
tray icon.
.PP
Distributing a compiled CastMirror binary linked against GPL-licensed libx264
generally requires treating that binary as GPL. See the NOTICE file shipped
with the source.
